{
  "info": {
    "name": "DemoQA Interview Demo - Account and BookStore",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "QA workflow demo: API contract analysis → test-case design → automation → execution → investigation → reporting.\n\nRun the folders in order (Collection Runner or Newman). Each run creates ONE disposable fictional user, exercises it, and deletes it in \"4 - Cleanup\".\n\nTest names start with the designed case ID (e.g. \"API-AC-001 | ...\") from test-cases/test-cases.csv.\n\nContract notes and documented-vs-observed discrepancies: test-cases/api-observed-behavior.md. API-CT-* tests check the documented contract and are expected to fail until the API or its documentation is aligned.\n\nSecrets: the password and token are generated at runtime into the environment CURRENT value only, never written to this file, and cleared at the end of the run."
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1 - Account lifecycle",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create User",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/Account/v1/User",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "Account",
                "v1",
                "User"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"userName\": \"{{username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Cases: API-AC-001, API-CT-001"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Start of the lifecycle: clear every value an earlier run may have left, so nothing stale is reused.",
                  "['username', 'userId', 'userPassword', 'authToken', 'selectedIsbn', 'selectedTitle'].forEach(k => pm.environment.unset(k));",
                  "// Username generated ONCE per lifecycle; every later request reuses it.",
                  "pm.environment.set('username', 'dqa_demo_' + Date.now() + '_' + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8));",
                  "// Disposable password meeting the confirmed rules (OBS-API-02): 8+ chars, upper, lower, digit, special.",
                  "// Stored only in the local environment's current value; never logged.",
                  "pm.environment.set('userPassword', 'Qa!' + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 10) + '7Z');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "let body;",
                  "try { body = pm.response.json(); } catch (e) { body = undefined; }",
                  "const UUID = /^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/;",
                  "// Assertions follow the OBSERVED contract (OBS-API-01). API-CT-001 checks the DOCUMENTED field separately (D1).",
                  "pm.test('API-AC-001 | status is 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('API-AC-001 | body has userID (UUID), username and books', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.be.an('object').that.has.all.keys('userID', 'username', 'books');",
                  "  pm.expect(UUID.test(body.userID), 'userID is a UUID').to.be.true;",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('API-AC-001 | username equals the requested username', () => pm.expect(body.username).to.eql(pm.environment.get('username')));",
                  "pm.test('API-AC-001 | new user starts with no books', () => pm.expect(body.books).to.eql([]));",
                  "pm.test('API-CT-001 | documented field \"userId\" is present (Swagger CreateUserResult)', () => pm.expect(body).to.have.property('userId'));",
                  "// Capture the identifier only after the success checks hold.",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201 && body && UUID.test(body.userID) && body.username === pm.environment.get('username')) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('userId', body.userID);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Generate Token",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/Account/v1/GenerateToken",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "Account",
                "v1",
                "GenerateToken"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"userName\": \"{{username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Cases: API-AC-002"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Prerequisite guard: skip (reported as not run) instead of sending a request with missing or stale data.",
                  "if (!pm.environment.get('userId') || !pm.environment.get('userPassword')) { pm.execution.skipRequest(); }"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "let body;",
                  "try { body = pm.response.json(); } catch (e) { body = undefined; }",
                  "const JWT = /^[\\w-]+\\.[\\w-]+\\.[\\w-]+$/;",
                  "pm.test('API-AC-002 | status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "// HTTP 200 alone is not success here (see API-AC-102), so the status field is asserted too.",
                  "pm.test('API-AC-002 | status is \"Success\" with the success message', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('Success');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.result).to.eql('User authorized successfully.');",
                  "});",
                  "// Boolean form keeps the token value out of failure messages and logs.",
                  "pm.test('API-AC-002 | token is a JWT', () => pm.expect(typeof body.token === 'string' && JWT.test(body.token), 'token has JWT shape').to.be.true);",
                  "pm.test('API-AC-002 | expires is a future date', () => pm.expect(Date.parse(body.expires) > Date.now(), 'expires is in the future').to.be.true);",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200 && body && body.status === 'Success' && JWT.test(body.token || '')) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('authToken', body.token);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Authorized",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
